1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Large language models are good at generating trading ideas.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
The problem is that they can also be confidently wrong.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
In options trading, one bad strike or one missed risk calculation
can put real capital in danger.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
This is 13forge. It lets AI propose an idea,
but it does not let AI place the trade.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Every order has to pass through deterministic Rust safety gates
before Alpaca is ever contacted.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Here, the AI suggests an oversized iron condor.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The system checks governor state, position state, model verdict,
market stability, trade structure, and maximum loss.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Then it computes the real downside.

9
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:53,000
A twenty-nine point wing, minus a three dollar and seventy-five cent credit,
creates a maximum loss of two thousand five hundred twenty-five dollars.

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The account limit is two thousand dollars.

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,000
So 13forge refuses the order.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The broker step stays locked. Alpaca is never reached.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,800
13forge: creative AI, deterministic control.
